00:03:44.720 --> 00:03:48.520
You know, I lost all immersion at that point.

00:03:48.720 --> 00:03:53.980
Absolutely. And what you guys are talking about is back to the reference of the back of the box.

00:03:54.180 --> 00:03:56.760
It took 2000 years for someone to make chess better.

00:03:57.120 --> 00:03:59.920
Better means that it has animation now.

00:03:59.920 --> 00:04:01.680
That is what they changed here.

00:04:01.820 --> 00:04:03.960
They didn't change the rules of chess at all.

00:04:04.060 --> 00:04:10.700
They didn't change how the pieces function or even an additional silly mode of chess.

00:04:10.860 --> 00:04:17.520
It is just this time the chess pieces can walk across the board.

00:04:17.760 --> 00:04:19.760
Granted, you have to still tell them where to go.

00:04:19.760 --> 00:04:32.020
But they'll walk across the board and then a fun little cut scene that is obviously predetermined based on, you know, who's capturing who will play out showing the combat.

00:04:32.020 --> 00:04:42.000
And to their credit, the animation is not just some dry, like, you know, soldiers on a battlefield striking one another.

00:04:42.140 --> 00:04:43.200
I mean, some of them are. Yeah, sure.

00:04:43.280 --> 00:04:53.220
And some of them are. But then occasionally, as referenced earlier, the king will just like pull out a gun or the golem will just eat you alive.

00:04:53.660 --> 00:04:55.480
The golem being the rook, of course.

00:04:55.480 --> 00:05:00.380
Everybody always thought that the rook was a golem, right?

00:05:01.520 --> 00:05:06.340
I mean, I guess it kind of is because it's like a living castle, right?

00:05:06.520 --> 00:05:13.360
That is weird. I never saw it that way or thought that it was like some kind of creepy otherly being.

00:05:13.800 --> 00:05:15.300
I mean, I also never did.

00:05:15.420 --> 00:05:16.780
But I'm thinking about it now.

00:05:16.960 --> 00:05:21.460
Why is it the only thing that's not a living person?

00:05:22.920 --> 00:05:32.880
Well, you know, from the, like the canon, like the deep lore of chess, that's just sort of how castles are built.

00:05:33.040 --> 00:05:41.180
Like, you know, like in Game of Thrones, I haven't seen it, but I imagine that like there's a castle that walks around.

00:05:41.540 --> 00:05:42.400
Oh, right, right.

00:05:42.400 --> 00:05:53.460
But is there anything else missing or anything I'm missing in highlighting what makes battle chess specifically different than regular chess?

00:05:53.740 --> 00:05:56.360
There are, you know, there are no rule changes.

00:05:56.360 --> 00:06:01.480
So other than adding some fun little animations to the chess game, right?

00:06:01.600 --> 00:06:07.920
It would basically be like if they, I'm pretty sure we are going to play an NES Monopoly game at some point.

00:06:08.140 --> 00:06:12.200
