00:06:17.920 --> 00:06:18.920
If they battle.

00:06:19.060 --> 00:06:23.100
It really is a, like a kind of a misnomer title.

00:06:23.100 --> 00:06:36.460
Like, I thought that this was kind of going to be like Archon, in that it was going to be chess that, like, because it even, it cuts to a little cut scene when, when you interact.

00:06:36.460 --> 00:06:44.700
And that's like where Mike was talking about all of the ways that they can die or shoot people.

00:06:44.700 --> 00:06:54.320
Um, and for some reason I thought it was going to be similar to in Archon where it cuts to that little cut scene where you can actually fight.

00:06:54.600 --> 00:06:59.300
But then I guess that isn't chess anymore, but maybe it could have been battle chess.

00:06:59.820 --> 00:07:02.620
Yeah. Yeah, that's what I was thinking too.

00:07:02.800 --> 00:07:07.920
I mean, like Archon, as much as it looks like a version of chess, it's not.

00:07:08.060 --> 00:07:09.060
The rules aren't like chess.

00:07:09.060 --> 00:07:10.040
It's got its own strategy.

00:07:10.160 --> 00:07:11.060
It's got its own rules.

00:07:11.220 --> 00:07:17.540
It's own game. I thought it would be kind of cool to have a game that has the rules of chess in some way.

00:07:18.440 --> 00:07:27.480
But, like, the defender, you know, if, if, if a pawn is about to take the, you know, your queen, then, like, the queen might have some advantage.

00:07:27.620 --> 00:07:36.980
Like, maybe, even though, even though the pawn, like, got the, the jump on her because of, like, the positioning, maybe there's some way you can, like, take control in the battle and there's stats or whatever.

00:07:37.060 --> 00:07:38.980
Like, that would make it different than regular chess.

00:07:38.980 --> 00:07:41.120
And I'm not saying that that would even be fun.

00:07:41.420 --> 00:07:51.560
Like, that might, like, I might hate that, but what, I, I think that a, a, a, a more apt title to this game would be, like, uh, illustrated chess.

00:07:52.100 --> 00:07:54.480
Yeah. Um, yeah.

00:07:54.540 --> 00:08:04.920
And it is cool, like, that they had to program, like, a scenario for every possible combination of people battling, I guess.

00:08:04.920 --> 00:08:07.720
Knight takes knight, knight takes bishop, yada yada.

00:08:07.720 --> 00:08:11.320
Exactly, yeah. And they have, they have a nice little different fun thing each time.

00:08:11.460 --> 00:08:23.100
But, you know, the problem being is that it's fun to watch the first time to see what's going to happen, how they're going to make it, you know, look like the, yeah, the, the pawn takes a rook or whatever.

00:08:23.100 --> 00:08:28.100
But then after that, it's like, okay, now I want to play chess.

00:08:28.440 --> 00:08:30.460
And it takes a long time.

