00:21:14.080 --> 00:21:15.360
So, it was just kind of ubiquitous.

00:21:15.360 --> 00:21:21.420
It was like, for the video gamer who needs chess, we've got you covered.

00:21:21.420 --> 00:21:39.840
Because you're on the Amiga, the 3DO, something called the Archimedes, the CD32, the CDTV, the Apple IIGS, the Atari ST, the Commodore 64, the FM Towns, the PC-98.

00:21:39.920 --> 00:21:42.280
That's what I was waiting to hear, the FM Towns.

00:21:42.500 --> 00:21:44.380
You knew it was coming to FM Towns.

00:21:44.420 --> 00:21:48.640
Absolutely. So, what would you do with Battle Chess 2?

00:21:48.780 --> 00:21:50.140
And, spoiler alert, there is one.

00:21:50.140 --> 00:22:02.500
So, if you were Interplay and you were hugely successful with Battle Chess, what would Battle Chess 2 be, knowing that you already did Battle Chess Enhanced with, like, a, you know, graphical overhaul?

00:22:03.060 --> 00:22:08.820
I would have Battle Chess with different, like, quirky ways of playing chess.

00:22:08.920 --> 00:22:10.500
And I'm not talking about what we were talking about before.

00:22:10.780 --> 00:22:15.960
But, like, there's a, I don't remember what it's called, but there's a way to play chess where you have two chess boards.

00:22:16.540 --> 00:22:19.000
And two people are, you know, two people are playing.

00:22:19.000 --> 00:22:30.100
And if you take the white queen, then that white queen goes to the other white player playing the other side.

00:22:30.320 --> 00:22:37.020
So, you can have, everyone's always trading pieces to these two games, and then whichever color wins both games ends up winning.

00:22:37.160 --> 00:22:39.840
And it's called Battle Chess 2 boards.

00:22:40.620 --> 00:22:41.860
Yes. Love it.

00:22:42.100 --> 00:22:43.040
That's interesting.

00:22:43.040 --> 00:22:54.300
I think. No, I would make each, like, I think that there would just be regular chess, and it would just be this game with the really slow animations.

00:22:54.300 --> 00:23:01.460
But there's a second mode where you can just pick a piece to be, like, a Tamagotchi.

00:23:02.780 --> 00:23:04.520
And you, like, feed them.

00:23:05.800 --> 00:23:13.920
And, like, if it's, you can, like, have little, like, there's little mini games where you can, like, scratch their chin.

00:23:14.840 --> 00:23:16.140
I think that'd be pretty cool.

00:23:16.880 --> 00:23:24.920
And if we're going Tamagotchi, I think it would be cool that if you could, like, yeah, you have a little, you're taking care of a little pawn, and then it'll, like, eventually evolve into, like, a bishop.

00:23:25.260 --> 00:23:28.780
Or, like, alternatively, it'll evolve into a rook, and eventually you get it to be a queen.

00:23:28.780 --> 00:23:30.800
No, no, no. You raise it.

00:23:30.860 --> 00:23:31.940
Pawns are lowborn.

00:23:32.720 --> 00:23:34.860
They will never become kings and queens.

00:23:35.120 --> 00:23:36.220
Well, they could become knights.

00:23:37.100 --> 00:23:38.400
Sure. Yeah.

00:23:38.720 --> 00:23:40.800
And then maybe something else becomes something else.

00:23:43.480 --> 00:23:46.620
Or maybe it could become, like, a weird duck thing, like Tamagotchi's did.

00:23:46.960 --> 00:23:48.020
Battle Chess 2.

00:23:49.420 --> 00:23:52.760
Abandoned traditional chess for Chinese chess.

00:23:53.680 --> 00:23:54.720
Chinese chess?

00:23:54.940 --> 00:23:55.960
Chinese chess.

00:23:56.200 --> 00:23:57.960
I believe it's called Jiang Qi.

00:23:58.780 --> 00:24:01.940
Which is also just known as Chinese chess here in the West.

00:24:03.060 --> 00:24:09.300
But it's just a completely, it's the same idea, same, like, you know, hey, let's add all these fun animations and everything.

00:24:09.680 --> 00:24:14.980
But hopefully they included a tutorial for this one, because I don't know about you guys, but I don't know the rules of Chinese chess.

00:24:15.600 --> 00:24:17.100
I definitely don't know the rules.

00:24:17.500 --> 00:24:18.580
They know that that was a thing.

00:24:18.660 --> 00:24:19.700
I know Chinese checkers.

00:24:20.900 --> 00:24:22.380
Yes, which was what I was wondering.

00:24:22.520 --> 00:24:25.000
I was like, is that what that is?

00:24:25.080 --> 00:24:25.900
But apparently, no.

00:24:26.140 --> 00:24:27.380
Chinese chess is different.

00:24:27.380 --> 00:24:31.080
And it's also different than Shogi, which is Japanese chess.

00:24:32.260 --> 00:24:36.800
Shogi I played thanks to Clubhouse 52 on Nintendo Switch.

00:24:37.020 --> 00:24:39.660
But never heard of Chinese chess before.

00:24:39.880 --> 00:24:41.100
I mean, I'll check it out. Why not?

00:24:41.520 --> 00:24:50.940
The problem with Chinese chess, at least in the game that they made, is that the board requires, like, a lot of different directions.

00:24:50.940 --> 00:24:54.860
It's not just a 64 square board.

00:24:55.100 --> 00:24:57.180
It, like, allows a lot of different ways.

00:24:57.660 --> 00:24:58.660
Is it, like, hex?

00:24:59.140 --> 00:25:00.940
No, no, no. It's still, it's still, sorry.

00:25:01.040 --> 00:25:02.200
It's still a square board.

00:25:02.340 --> 00:25:07.060
But I just mean, like, you can walk in a lot of different directions depending on where you are.

00:25:07.100 --> 00:25:08.920
And then you can only walk forward.

00:25:08.920 --> 00:25:11.720
And then you can start walking in a bunch of different directions again.

00:25:11.720 --> 00:25:19.220
I don't like that. So everything got, like, in order to fit it on the screen, everything got kind of, like, scrunched in, which makes everything look really stretched.

00:25:20.780 --> 00:25:22.500
Which is just not a good decision.

00:25:22.720 --> 00:25:25.760
Instead, there's got to be another way to emulate that.

00:25:25.760 --> 00:25:29.280
But I've never seen another version of Chinese chess done on video games.

00:25:29.280 --> 00:25:34.520
So maybe this is just a, this is the great barrier for humanity or for civilization.

00:25:34.540 --> 00:25:38.220
Nobody has been able to put Chinese chess on a video game.

00:25:38.320 --> 00:25:40.300
And that's usually what collapses society.

